    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0486" n="370" xml:id="pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1174</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chilean Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mathieu</hi>)<anchor n="71" xml:id="d236-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: With reference to my notes of March
                    13, 1923, and September 17, 1923,<anchor n="72" xml:id="d236-f2"/> and in
                    compliance with the agreement made between you and the Peruvian Ambassador
                    regarding the conducting of the arbitration arranged between both parties on
                    July 20, 1922, as set forth in your note No. 53, of March 2, 1923,<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d236-f3"/> I now have the honor, on behalf of the President, to hand
                    you herewith the case of Peru, in two volumes, and to inform you that there will
                    be a period of three months from today in which to reply thereto, and that this
                    period may be extended for two months more should either party so request.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d236-f1" n="71" type="source" xml:id="d236-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Peruvian
                    Chargé.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d236-f2" n="72" xml:id="d236-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d236-f3" n="73" xml:id="d236-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; see Department’s instruction of Mar. 21 to the Chargé in Peru.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
